.TH NPTE 8 "@DATE@" "npte @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
npte \- Network Performance Testing Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B npte
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B npte
tests how a network client behaves on a realistic access link by
building isolated Linux network namespaces, wiring them together
with veth pairs, and shaping the resulting links with
.BR tc (8)
and
.BR tc-netem (8).
No real hardware or second machine is required.
.PP
The tool is a collection of small, composable subcommands:
.B netns
creates and connects namespaces;
.B gateway
attaches a host\-NATed uplink to a namespace;
.B netem
applies and clears link shaping;
.B container
runs commands inside a
.BR systemd-nspawn (1)
container;
.B lab
wires a fixed client/router/server topology for the common case;
and
.B mcp
speaks the Model Context Protocol over stdio, exposing the
.BR netns ", " netem ", and " lab
primitives to a coding agent that cannot shell to
.BR sudo (8).
.PP
Most subcommands require root and exec external utilities such as
.BR ip (8),
.BR tc (8),
.BR iptables (8),
.BR sysctl (8),
.BR systemd-nspawn (1),
.BR debootstrap (8),
and
.BR runuser (1).
Run
.B npte doctor
to check which of these are present on the host.
.SH EXAMPLES
For the full list of commands and per\-command help, run:
.PP
.RS 4
.B npte \-\-help
.br
.BI "npte " command " \-\-help"
.RE
.PP
For an interactive walkthrough \(em basic namespaces, routing,
.BR tc-netem (8)
shaping, bufferbloat experiments, browsers, containers \(em run:
.PP
.RS 4
.B npte tutorial
.RE
.PP
To allowlist the
.BR netns ", " netem ", and " lab
subcommands for passwordless
.BR sudo (8)
on the invoking user's account, run:
.PP
.RS 4
.B npte sudoers
.RE
.PP
The output is a sudoers snippet ready to paste via
.BR visudo (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ip (8),
.BR ip-netns (8),
.BR tc (8),
.BR tc-netem (8),
.BR iptables (8),
.BR systemd-nspawn (1),
.BR debootstrap (8),
.BR sudoers (5)
